lookCopyT -- popups stroke 0 (SEQ 762, 2026-11-23; F-158; Tony's ruling via Clay): the look rides on the laid-out copy. setFrame
leaves the look it resolved through on the copy's top as laidLook (a holder to the look, or the word none), a held form's top too;
typeset, at draw, climbs from the field it is drawing to the nearest laidLook and resolves a run's placeholders through that, not
through the look of whichever layout ran last. Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh, run at GCSTRESS=1000. No window is shown.

night / day / night again   two offscreen windows, lcFormN under lcNight (accent red) and lcFormD under lcDay (accent green), each
          with a run naming color:=accent. Pixel (84,10) is inside the run. The night window is read again after the day window
          was laid out: until this stroke its run turned green and 470 of 30000 pixels differed.
third     firstLight in a third window (defaultLook, accent red), clicked: the day window read again; then resized and clicked
          again: the day window read once more. Both equal its first read, the run still green.
hostA     lcHostA under look="dark" holds lcHeld, whose list has standard only: lcHeld falls back to its own standard (accent
          blue). SPAN lines print the last text drawn, lcHeld's: its run is blue, its own look's, not the host's green.
hostB     the same with the held field first, so the last text drawn is the host's: its run is the host's green.
plain     a form naming no placeholder of its own, no look: laidLook none; the run is defaultLook's red.
nightPdf  the PDF road under a look field: laidLook is lcNight.
definition  the definitions carry no laidLook.
